7f7b3-c443-428d-9545-6025f4c690fe","position":{"commit_sha":"fc9ecdfbdc5d1b2b5e0001c127cc76f34c8df484","position":"1787081971524598001-9067f7b3-c443-428d-9545-6025f4c690fe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"746ad80a818b7345206e327eaa46d5f310d8b22451bef38168ef07f36390e516","event_uuid":"5949b5d8-344b-4fc4-9048-8afb4daa1ab8","position":{"commit_sha":"6ad24148baf9544f8a47ab3582688276783e5d2c","position":"1787082944530645001-5949b5d8-344b-4fc4-9048-8afb4daa1ab8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787080925392033001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0503c455-5e7c-4b2a-ac05-95e01a74a113","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"}],"description":"Standardize the CLI write-command argument parsing: retire the hand-rolled manual loop for Python's stdlib argparse, WITHOUT changing observable behavior.\n\n## Context / Problem\nToday the CLI parses write-command args with a hand-rolled loop (src/rebar/_commands/claim.py _parse_force/_parse_assignee, plus the transition path) carrying bespoke semantics not reflected in any schema: a bare --force yields the default reason \"(no reason given)\"; --assignee ABSENT is a None sentinel (=> ticket.default_assignee fallback) while explicit --assignee \"\" CLEARS the assignee. This is tech-debt: flags and --help can silently drift from actual behavior.\n\n## Approach\nRefactor the CLI write-command parsing onto Python's stdlib argparse. argparse is the chosen default: zero new runtime dependency and portable, and it generates accurate --help; we do NOT adopt Click or Typer, to avoid adding a runtime dependency. This is a behavior-preserving ADAPTER REFACTOR, orthogonal to the parity oracle. Respect the module-size (<=800 LOC) and per-function complexity ratchets by extracting along existing call-graph seams rather than inflating a single function.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/claim.py — replace the _parse_force/_parse_assignee hand loop with argparse, preserving the sentinel semantics.\n- The transition CLI arg path (src/rebar/_commands/transition.py or the equivalent transition command module) — same treatment.\n- Lib and MCP surfaces are OUT OF SCOPE (this is an adapter-local change).\n\n## Contract preservation (must not regress)\nFlag spellings, exit-code 10 (ConcurrencyError), the bare-`--force` default-reason semantics, and the --assignee None-vs-empty-string distinction must be preserved exactly.\n\n## Testing\n- Existing CLI interface tests pass unchanged (tests/interfaces).\n- Bare `--force` still yields reason \"(no reason given)\"; `--force=<r>` yields <r> (test).\n- --assignee absent => default_assignee fallback; --assignee \"\" => cleared (test asserts both).\n- A ConcurrencyError still exits 10.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CLI write-command parsing goes through argparse and `--help` is generated (verified by running the command's --help and confirming it lists the flags).\n- [ ] Bare `--force` default-reason and `--force=<r>` explicit-reason semantics are preserved (test).\n- [ ] The --assignee None-vs-empty-string distinction is preserved: absent => default_assignee fallback, \"\" => cleared (test asserts both).\n- [ ] Exit code 10 on ConcurrencyError is preserved (existing CLI interface tests pass).\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` are green; module-size and complexity ratchets respected.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","reason":"replace hand-rolled _parse_force/_parse_assignee loop with argparse"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"standardize transition CLI arg parsing onto argparse"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fd48-7a80-33e9-4400","ticket_type":"story","title":"Standardize CLI write-command arg parsing (retire hand-rolled loop for a std framework)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["74c4c275-48ad-4fd4-a706-f68cd21394fc","0503c455-5e7c-4b2a-ac05-95e01a74a113","c66fee65-6b8f-40b1-a465-2013d7b97702","9067f7b3-c443-428d-9545-6025f4c690fe","5949b5d8-344b-4fc4-9048-8afb4daa1ab8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787082944530645002,"uuid":"498a84bd-5548-4845-90d1-b0b311f100ed"}